{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98528","id":2146405748,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc5_7410","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98528","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98528.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98528.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98528","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98528/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98528/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98528/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/dda0c4c24518ea3bf25dcdbbed2df2ee8b2be8a3","number":98528,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Separate Godot Physics (advanced) project settings from generic physics project settings","user":{"login":"rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229837?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing","html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This is to avoid having a bunch of seemingly generic (advanced) project settings that actually have no effect in other physics server implementations (coming from modules/GDExtensions like Jolt, Box2D, Rapier, etc.).\r\n\r\nThese Godot Physics specific (advanced) settings are moved from `Physics / 2D` and `Physics / 3D` to `Physics / Godot Physics 2D` and `Physics / Godot Physics 3D` respectively. This is consistent with how existing GDExtensions like Jolt, Box2D and Rapier store their implementation-specific settings.\r\n\r\n**Preserves compatibility** by moving the old setting's value (if it exists and the new setting does not yet have a value) to the new setting (and removing the old setting).\r\n\r\nNote: currently all the Godot Physics specific settings are marked \"advanced\" (as they probably should be).\r\n\r\nNote: *reading* any of these (advanced) settings in a script using `ProjectSettings.get_setting` with the old setting name will obviously fail, but this is such a corner case that I doubt anyone is doing that with these advanced settings (including physics enthusiasts).","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":955079684,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw5NTUwNzk2ODQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/breaks%20compat","name":"breaks compat","description":"","color":"b64245","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godo